# Credentials for the scheduled brief's optional lanes.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/deepsearch/env, fill in, and chmod 600. run-local.sh
# sources that path when it exists; the harness scripts read these directly.
# Nothing here is required — a lane whose credentials are absent reports itself
# unavailable and the brief carries on without it.
#
# This file is checked in as a template ONLY. Never commit the filled copy.

# --- Bluesky ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The public appview refuses unauthenticated reads from many regions (403 from
# KR), so the authenticated API is the only reliable path.
# Issue an APP PASSWORD, not your account password:
#   Settings -> Privacy and security -> App passwords -> Add App Password
# An app password can be revoked on its own and cannot change your account.
BLUESKY_HANDLE=
BLUESKY_APP_PASSWORD=

# --- Reddit ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The unauthenticated .json endpoints return 403 to datacenter and scripted
# traffic. A free "script" app lifts that:
#   https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps -> create app -> type: script
# The client id is the string under the app name; the secret is labelled.
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Semantic Scholar (optional) -------------------------------------------
# The papers lane works anonymously but is rate-limited. A free key raises it:
#   https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api#api-key
SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY=

# --- GitHub ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately absent. `gh` is authenticated on this machine and
# search_github.py prefers it, so a PAT here would add a second credential to
# rotate and leak for no gain. Only set GITHUB_TOKEN if `gh` stops being an
# option, and never on a host where the environment is visible to others.
